      <div type="clause" n="15">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Rect">Rect</ref> 15</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="451" ed="#liebermann"/>[15] Be gathyrde. Gathyrde gebyreð his heorde meolc ofer Martinus mæssedæig, ⁊ ær ðam his dæl hwæges ⁊ I ticcen of geares geogoðe, gif he his heorde wel begymeð.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="451" ed="#liebermann"/>Caprario conuenit lac gregis sui post festum sancti Martini, et antea pars sui mesguii et unum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Rect_15.lnote.oe.10"/> capritum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#Rect_15.lnote.oe.c"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Rect_15.lnote.oe.11"/> anniculum, si bene custodiat gregem suum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#gobbitt" n="16" corresp="#wit-b">Be Gat hyrde . Gathyrde gebyreð his heorde meolc ofer martinus mæssedæig . 7 ær ðam his dæl hwæges .7 i. ticcen . of geares geo|goðe gif he his heorde wel begymeð.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="328" ed="#rabin-doml"/><hi rend="italic">Be gathyrde</hi> Gathyrde gebyreð his heorde meolc ofer Martinus mæssedæig, and ær ðam his dæl hwæges, and I ticcen of geares geogoðe, gif he his heorde wel begymeð.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="451" ed="#liebermann"/>Vom Ziegenhirten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Rect_15.lnote.de.1"/>. Dem Ziegenhirten gebührt die Milch seiner<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#Rect_15.lnote.de1.e"/> Herde nach Martinus' Festtag, und vorher sein Theil<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="g" target="#Rect_15.lnote.de1.g"/> Molken und ein Zicklein<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="h" target="#Rect_15.lnote.de1.h"/> vom Jungvieh des Jahres, wenn er seine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#Rect_15.lnote.de1.e-2"/> Herde wohl besorgt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of the goatherd. To the goatherd is due the milk of his herd after Martinmas, and before that his share of whey and one kid of the year's young, if he cares for his herd well.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#gobbitt" corresp="#wit-b">Concerning the goatherd To the goatherd is due his herd’s milk on Martin’s Mass day, and before then his portion of whey, and one kid from the year’s young if he has looked after his herd well.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="329" ed="#rabin-doml"/><hi rend="italic">Regarding the Goatherd</hi> To the goatherd is due the milk of his herd after the Feast of Saint Martin, and before that his share of whey, and one kid from the year’s young if he looks after his herd well.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares Rect 14 and 7.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_15.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">451</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_15.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">451</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Lex Sal.</hi> 5, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Lex Sal.</hi> 5, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_15.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">451</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-icum agnic. <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-icum agnic. MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Rect_15.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">251</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Ziege 1. 5. Man ass Zicklein; Round <hi rend="italic">aaO</hi>. 368. Es scheinen Ziegenmolken gemeint</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Ziege 1. 5. Kids were eaten; Round <hi rend="italic">loc. cit</hi>. 368. Goats' whey seems to be meant</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Rect_15.lnote.de1.e" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">451</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 4, 2<hi rend="italic">d</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> 4, 2<hi rend="italic">d</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Rect_15.lnote.de1.g" n="g" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">451</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">wohl wie in</hi> 14</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">probably as in 14</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Rect_15.lnote.de1.h" n="h" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">451</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 7</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> 7</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Rect_15.lnote.de1.e-2" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">451</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 4, 2<hi rend="italic">d</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> 4, 2<hi rend="italic">d</hi></seg></note>
